            // Source-plane resolution for every vendor package tsconfig.host.json
    // registers for dsh-typert-generator own sake (originally just
    // @deepseek-ai/dsh-typert-protocol; widened at vendor pin 841f76d3 --
    // see tsconfig.host.json own comment for the full story). The
    // generator own analysis builds ONE shared ts.Program whose rootNames
    // already include every registered package own SOURCE file directly;
    // an ordinary bare-specifier import of that same package from a
    // DIFFERENT file still resolves it the normal way, through
    // node_modules built .d.ts -- a SEPARATE file object from the rootName
    // source, so the generator sees the SAME declare-module merge twice
    // ("duplicate ... key") or compares two distinct symbol identities
    // across a cross-package heritage/binding check ("is not exported by"
    // or an outright TypeScript checker crash). These entries make every
    // such import resolve to the SAME source file the rootName already
    // uses. Extend this map only for a package tsconfig.host.json
    // registers for the generators sake -- not a general source-plane
    // substitute. Entries were generated by resolving every ./lib/...
    // export target of each registered vendor package.json (stripping an
    // explicit tsconfig*.json suffix first, for a dual host/client-face
    // package) to its ./src/... source equivalent; regenerate the same way
    // after adding or removing a tsconfig.host.json registration.
